{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>By Me.</b> The sense of \"by Me\" is that He exists, and every place where there is an oath, it is a decree that has been decreed and shall not be annulled." "<b>[Righteousness] has gone out from My mouth.</b> A word of righteousness, like \"righteousness from me\" (Genesis 38:26), and the sense is a word of truth." "<b>For to Me, etc.</b> And the sense is: these future things I will do, until every knee bends to Me, every tongue swears to be Mine, for to Me — He draws after, according to rule, וכמוהו \"and in His name you swear\" (Deuteronomy 6:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {1 "The bracketed [צדקה] appears to reflect a variant reading or reconstruction of the lemma; the received Hebrew text of Isaiah 45:23 reads דבר־צדקה.", 2 "The phrase 'He draws after, according to rule' is elliptic; translated hyper-literally as the syntax offers no explicit subject or object."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:17.921848519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}